+# Execution, process attachment and bounded queues
+
+Audit the actual command, inputs, helper and host capabilities before use. Permissions
+remain mandatory. This package does not install a daemon, scheduler, OpenCode server,
+network endpoint or privileged process debugger. Its optional queue is a finite
+foreground CLI using Node built-ins and POSIX process groups, one job at a time.
+
+## Three different meanings of attach
+
+1. **OpenCode backend:** `opencode attach` connects a terminal to an existing OpenCode
+   server. `opencode run --attach` sends work through a running server. Verify the
+   installed CLI/help, server identity, project directory and authentication first.
+   Do not expose a server on a public interface or auto-change permissions for this.
+2. **Host execution session:** when an actual tool returns a persistent terminal/job/
+   session ID, retain it and use that tool's documented resume/output/wait operation.
+   Do not invent a tool name or relaunch the operation because the invocation yielded.
+3. **This package's queue observer:** `execution-queue.mjs attach` observes the explicit
+   run directory's state. It does not attach a debugger, send stdin, adopt arbitrary
+   PIDs, take over another shell, or connect to an OpenCode server.
+
+If the host cannot retain an execution session, use an explicitly opened terminal
+or an existing authorized supervisor. Otherwise report that persistent execution is
+unavailable. Do not append an uncontrolled `&`, fabricate a session ID or promise that
+a process will continue after the host kills its execution environment.
+
+## Execution lifecycle and waiting
+
+Record project root, task/run IDs, exact reviewed argv, working directory, source and
+plan fingerprints, start time, deadline, process identity, logs and terminal result.
+Separate process state from task verification. The queue uses child `close` events,
+not a fixed sleep, to advance after process/stdio completion. A failed dependency
+skips its dependent checks; independent checks in the same approved task may still
+run sequentially to collect diagnostics. Cancellation skips remaining work.
+
+Keep one shared-state writer. A supported persistent host session may allow the agent
+to perform independent read-only analysis for the current task while checks run.
+Do not start an unrelated feature, race shared files, oversubscribe resources, or
+mutate inputs while validating them. Resource/source changes invalidate evidence.
+No queue-empty observation, silent log, PID disappearance or exit 0 alone proves the
+application outcome. For real external queues inspect producer status, in-flight,
+retry, delayed and dead-letter work, acknowledgement/commit semantics and required
+persisted results. This helper is not an adapter for arbitrary external queues.
+
+The observer uses filesystem state-change notifications and a bounded deadline. It
+returns control when the run finishes or the observation window expires; an observer
+timeout does not cancel or restart a job. Prefer native completion events. When only
+status polling is available elsewhere, use bounded backoff and an overall deadline,
+not a busy loop or repeated fixed sleeps. Record WAITING/BLOCKED and stop safely if
+the actual environment cannot continue.
+
+## Implemented files and interfaces
+
+- `.opencode/scripts/execution-queue.mjs`: explicit `run` or read-only `attach`.
+- `.opencode/lib/execution-queue.mjs`: foreground single-writer supervisor and observer.
+- `.opencode/scripts/work-evidence.mjs`: read-only `check`, `due`, `contract`, `mermaid`.
+- `.opencode/lib/work-evidence.mjs`: bounded data/schema, task contract and evidence checks.
+- `.opencode/scripts/skill-audit.mjs`: existing audit helper, now with byte `compare`.
+
+These are local scripts, not new built-in OpenCode tools. Run them through an actual
+permitted execution capability only after reviewing their source/dependencies. The
+skill-integrity registry remains a separate authority and is not populated by them.
+
+## Ledger v1
+
+Use an existing tracker first. If a JSON evidence sidecar is needed, choose its path
+explicitly; the helpers have no automatic ledger discovery or creation. Start from
+`.opencode/docs/templates/work-ledger.example.json`, which is intentionally empty and
+UNCONFIGURED. Do not ship or copy a fixture ledger as installation approval.
+
+Required ledger fields:
+- `schema_version: 1`, exact canonical `project_root`, non-placeholder `context_id`.
+- `review_policy.interval_hours`: configured 1..8760 hours, evaluated at invoked checkpoints.
+- `goals`: unique `{id, title}` records.
+- `tasks`: unique `{id, title, kind, status, goal_ids, dependencies, inputs, acceptance}`.
+
+`kind` is `code`, `documentation`, or `analysis`. Status is TODO, IN_PROGRESS, WAITING,
+BLOCKED, DONE, or CANCELLED. IDs start with an ASCII letter and contain only letters,
+digits, underscores or hyphens, up to 64 characters. `acceptance` contains one or more
+`{id, description}` records. `inputs` lists the actual source/test/config/lockfiles
+whose contents matter; use canonical project-relative paths without symlinks, `..`,
+absolute paths or backslashes. Include the relevant dependency closure, not just the
+edited file. Dynamic ledger status and output receipts must not be their own inputs.
+
+Optional `last_reviewed_at` and `next_review_at` use UTC ISO timestamps, not ambiguous
+local clock strings. BLOCKED requires a concrete `blocker`. Preserve other tracker
+metadata, original completion claims and reopening reasons in the authoritative tracker.
+
+A DONE claim also needs:
+```json
+{
+  "verification": {
+    "reviewer": "actual reviewer identity",
+    "reviewed_at": "actual UTC timestamp after the observed run",
+    "rationale": "why the observed checks establish these acceptance criteria",
+    "receipt": {"path": "relative/run-directory/run.json", "sha256": "actual receipt SHA-256"}
+  }
+}
+```
+This is a field-shape illustration, not valid completed evidence. Never paste these
+placeholders as approval. Review test relevance and actual results before writing it.
+Code tasks need a relevant behavioral/unit/integration/runtime check, not static-only
+success. The helper also verifies matching task/goal/criteria contract, project context,
+plan, producer source revision, declared input hashes, captured logs and chronology.
+Review expiry is an additional stale signal. Missing evidence cannot become a pass.
+
+## Execution plan v1
+
+A plan has `schema_version: 1`, `max_concurrency: 1`, `max_log_bytes` (128..1048576 per
+stream per job), and 1..128 jobs. Each job specifies:
+`id`, `kind` (`static`, `unit`, `integration`, `runtime`), `argv` (array beginning with
+an inspected absolute executable path), `cwd` (explicit relative directory; `.` means
+project root), `timeout_ms` (1..600000), `depends_on` (job IDs), and `covers` (acceptance
+IDs). Validate each argv against the actual installed tool and scripts. No shell
+string, PATH guessing, implicit environment override or unsupported option is accepted.
+The static dependency DAG must be acyclic and cover every criterion.
+
+The runner is for reviewed finite checks, not interactive shells, daemon launchers,
+automatic deployments or retries. Spawn uses `shell:false` with a separate owned POSIX
+process group for cleanup. Commands still execute arbitrary reviewed project code and
+inherit the environment; this is NOT a sandbox. Inspect test/build hooks and control
+network access using the actual environment, not an imaginary runner security policy.
+
+## Invocation example
+
+All paths below are placeholders to replace with verified local paths. Prepare the
+ledger and check plan by inspecting the actual project. The output parent must already
+exist; every run directory must be new. A repeated output directory is rejected to
+prevent duplicate execution. This is deliberate, not a failed idempotent install.
+
+```sh
+TOOLS="/absolute/path/to/reviewed/package/.opencode/scripts"
+ROOT="/absolute/path/to/target/project"
+node "$TOOLS/work-evidence.mjs" due --root "$ROOT" --ledger production/session-state/work-ledger.json
+node "$TOOLS/work-evidence.mjs" check --root "$ROOT" --ledger production/session-state/work-ledger.json
+
+# Run once in a supported persistent host session or an explicit terminal.
+node "$TOOLS/execution-queue.mjs" run --root "$ROOT" \
+  --ledger production/session-state/work-ledger.json --task TASK_ID \
+  --plan production/session-state/check-plan.json \
+  --out production/session-state/runs/UNIQUE_RUN_ID --execute-reviewed-plan
+
+# Observe from another invocation. This never starts or repeats the operation.
+node "$TOOLS/execution-queue.mjs" attach --root "$ROOT" \
+  --out production/session-state/runs/UNIQUE_RUN_ID --wait-ms 1000
+```
+The explicit flag guards accidental execution; it is not proof of permission or a
+bypass of host approval. Do not repeatedly invoke `run` when you intend to observe.
+A real run exit 0 means SUCCEEDED execution only. Failed/cancelled/invalidated runs
+exit 2. `attach` returns its snapshot even when still RUNNING; inspect the JSON status
+and `wait_timed_out`, not merely the CLI exit. Attach wait is limited to 0..30000 ms.
+
+After a result, read and review the tests, logs and acceptance behavior. Only then
+update the authoritative task record with real evidence under authorization. The
+helper never updates DONE automatically. Re-run `check` after recording it.
+
+## Limits, failure and recovery
+
+Outputs are new private run directories (0700) with metadata/logs (0600). The supervisor
+atomically replaces its state file, captures bounded stdout/stderr, and stops an
+output-flooding job instead of treating truncated evidence as sufficient. Per-job
+timeouts and cancellation terminate the owned group, then escalate after a bounded
+grace period. Surviving owned descendants prevent a success claim. Jobs that detach
+into unrelated sessions or remote services are outside this supervisor's guarantees.
+
+Use SIGINT/SIGTERM on the actual foreground supervisor when cancellation is authorized.
+`attach` cannot kill a process. On Linux, the observer compares boot identity and the
+supervisor's process-start ticks to reduce PID-reuse confusion; a mismatch is LOST,
+not success or permission to adopt/kill/retry. Other platforms report liveness unverified.
+Windows process supervision is unsupported in v1; macOS/POSIX behavior needs local tests.
+No operating-system-wide discovery or reattachment to arbitrary PIDs is performed.
+
+File/path/hash checks assume one authorized writer and a non-hostile working directory.
+They do not eliminate TOCTOU races, cryptographically attest tests, redact secrets or
+prove the declared input list is complete. Do not print secrets in check commands or
+logs; restricted permissions are not redaction. Record external tool versions,
+configuration and environment evidence separately and change context when they change.
+No raw environment values are captured by the helper.
+
+The receipt binds the plan/task/producer and before/after declared inputs. Edits during
+a run, missing logs, wrong context, stale review or failed checks prevent a verified
+DONE claim. Newly added undeclared dependencies still require impact re-discovery.
+Do not copy approval records across projects. The global-versus-local OpenCode resolver
+limitation from `audit-runtime.md` remains until tested in the installed host.
+
+## Official contracts consulted 2026-09-28
+
+- https://opencode.ai/docs/cli/
+- https://nodejs.org/api/child_process.html
+
+Runtime results in the upgrade report are separate from these external references.
