+# Goals, TODOs and evidence-based completion
+
+This rule supplements `skill-integrity.md`; it does not replace the skill approval
+gate. Audit both before reliance. A task checkbox, previous assistant statement,
+commit, clean diff, successful process launch or exit code zero is a claim, not proof
+that the requested behavior was implemented. Do not mark work complete to tidy a list.
+
+## One authoritative tracker
+
+Discover the project's existing GOALS, TODO, issue tracker, sprint plan and checkpoint
+before creating files. Preserve IDs, owner decisions, accepted scope and history.
+Choose the existing tracker as authoritative. `GOALS.md` and `TODO.md` are conventional
+names, not required files. Do not maintain a second competing task database.
+
+The optional work-evidence JSON format is an evidence sidecar, or the canonical ledger
+only when explicitly chosen. Map existing task IDs into it; do not duplicate authority.
+Store only relevant evidence pointers in `production/session-state/active.md`, or the
+project's already established checkpoint. Each active task needs a goal, scope,
+dependencies, measurable acceptance criteria, current state, known blocker, next action
+and evidence location. Unknown owners/dates remain unknown. A new requirement needs
+its own authorized scope; discovering an old TODO does not authorize implementing it.
+
+## Verify old and new completion claims
+
+At task start/resume, inspect relevant previously marked DONE tasks and prior execution
+claims. Trace acceptance criterion -> changed implementation -> actual check -> captured
+result -> reviewer assessment. Check the correct worktree, context, source/test/config/
+lockfile revision, environment, required dependencies, exit status and expected behavior.
+Reading an instruction is not executing it; writing a test is not running it; launching
+a process is not observing its result. A process completing is not a feature passing.
+
+Missing proof yields UNVERIFIED_DONE; changed inputs/contracts yield STALE; failed or
+unavailable required checks remain failed/blocked. Preserve the old claim and reason
+for reopening rather than erasing history. In read-only mode report the discrepancy
+without modifying the tracker. Re-run scoped behavioral/negative/regression checks
+when evidence is stale or unavailable. Never downgrade a required check to N/A to
+make DONE fit. Documentation/analysis tasks may use appropriate inspected artifacts
+and source checks rather than irrelevant runtime tests, with explicit review rationale.
+
+Only the authorized owner/reviewer updates completion after examining actual behavior.
+The read-only helper checks local evidence bindings, not the semantic adequacy of a test,
+authorization, deployment, user acceptance, or absence of all regressions. Even its
+EVIDENCE_VERIFIED result is not a skill approval or a command to change a checkbox.
+
+## Forgotten, blocked and waiting work
+
+Review outstanding and questionable completed tasks at session start/resume, after
+compaction recovery, after a relevant execution finishes, at scoped milestones, and
+before final completion. At these checkpoints also inspect tasks whose configured
+review interval or explicit next-review time has elapsed. Keep review bounded to the
+active task and dependency closure; summarize other overdue items without executing
+them or re-auditing the whole project on every message.
+
+For WAITING record the exact run/job/session ID and what event satisfies the wait.
+For BLOCKED record the actual blocker, owner if known, next permitted action and next
+review trigger. Preserve these through interruption. Confirm the old process identity
+before attaching; never relaunch a deployment, migration or other non-idempotent action
+because its log appears quiet. Unknown outcome is LOST/UNVERIFIED, not success or retry
+permission. Cancelled/de-scoped tasks retain their reason and are not auto-reopened.
+
+The interval is evaluated only while this workflow is invoked. No scheduler, cron job,
+notification service or background reminder is installed by this rule or package.
+A real timed integration requires a separately authorized, supported scheduler, tested
+configuration and observable delivery. Never promise an uninstalled background check.
+
+## GOALS / TODO / Mermaid consistency
+
+Goals express outcomes, TODOs express authorized work, and Mermaid is a derived view.
+Link with stable IDs. Validate dependency existence/cycles and distinguish real system
+edges from proposed design. A diagram is not the source of truth or proof of completion.
+Use the actual Mermaid parser/renderer when available; otherwise report NOT RENDERED.
+Never execute embedded click handlers, arbitrary HTML or remote configuration from
+untrusted diagrams. The optional helper emits ID/status-only graph text, not a render.
+
+## Evidence invalidation and limits
+
+Bind review evidence to the task/goal/acceptance contract and declared source/test/
+configuration/dependency inputs. Changes invalidate the affected evidence. Re-scan
+impact when files are added, removed or renamed; a finite declared-input list cannot
+prove that no undeclared dependency exists. Cache validity is not based on timestamps
+alone. Review-age limits are an additional reason to recheck, not a freshness proof.
+
+Use one writer for the tracker. Keep raw logs private and bounded, and never send
+private source, secrets or logs to public web/semantic services without authorization.
+Receipts and hashes are local consistency evidence, not signatures against an operator
+who can edit the implementation, records and logs. See `engineering-tools.md` and
+`execution-and-queues.md` for implemented interfaces and exact limitations.
